    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_abb49118c78c191519a828f1e01bda4428d91462dcf4e2d468dab71c3413678e",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The proof isolates three budgets: oscillation controls the excluded low-height range, Fourier decay and clustering bound the denominator energy, and positivity turns the numerator into selected multiplicative coincidences carrying A_N gain. Once the first two losses are lower order for the chosen parameters, the numerator inherits the GCD-sum scale, and the authors use the general GCD bound and weighted-unweighted comparison to argue that this Soundararajan-style route can improve only the constant slightly.",
