    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_fc1f8ca8fd26407371c2324a792825ad3a7287febe7a53328ab645205926f2fa",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The optimized weighted GCD quotient Lambda acts as a relaxation of the uniform average Gamma; the comparison Lambda(N) <= (e^2+1)(log N+2) max_{n<=N} Gamma(n) forces a large uniform witness at some smaller index when Theorem 2 makes Lambda large, transferring weighted gain into arbitrarily large unweighted configurations and ruling out an upper-bound exponent below one.",
